{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1793696668,"nonce":"bf75zafaIpyUli8e3ucdyY8Al+U=","message":"Refined cause for method_call (NUC release, 4 CPUs). The size of the lowered chunk comes from polymorphic dispatch, not from method calls in general. Marginal lowered size of one statement in a script that defines both Toggle and NthToggle: t:value() (one target) 15 instructions, 6 blocks, 3 calls; t:activate() (activate is overridden, two targets) 63 instructions, 26 blocks, 5 calls; the same t:activate():value() in a script with one class: 30 instructions, 12 blocks. A site with two targets is lowered as a lookup-end selection (about 6 blocks of selects), an arm per target (call, pending-error check, return path, forwarding blocks) and a nil-callee fallback with its own raise and return. The two targets exist because the table made inside Toggle.new is later given the NthToggle metatable by NthToggle.new (setmetatable(o, NthToggle)), so the shape of a Toggle.new result has classes {Toggle, NthToggle} for every receiver; the types are flow-insensitive and have no way to say that main's t is only ever a plain Toggle. What precision is worth: method_call with the NthToggle class removed (every call single-target) runs 27 ms wall against 52, 1.6 ms elapsed against 7.8, and its chunk compiles in 10.1 ms against 24.0 (body 8.2 against 18.8). Directions, by size: (a) a leaner two-target dispatch (compare the metatable's shape directly in a chain instead of computing an end index and dispatching on it, one pending-error check after the arms join, no forwarding blocks), estimated 26 to about 14 blocks per site; (b) class-precise shapes for constructor results, so that a Toggle.new result at main's call site has class set {Toggle} and the result of NthToggle.new {NthToggle}: shapes would carry a class set apart from their layout, and Round's setmetatable handling would have to apply to the flow of one object, which is a project; (c) not interpreting the chunk first (moves the cost into the timed region). Also found and fixed on the way: 96270a5 (wrong result and SIGSEGV for an inherited method called on a second shape).","files":null}]}